  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1... \nEnsemble model analysis remains firm on upper ridging and\nsurface high pressure dominating the weather pattern over the\nupper Ohio River Valley for much of the next week plus. Any\ndaily variations arise from shifts on the center placement of\nthe high and/or passage of shortwaves north of the region. The\nresult is consistently above normal temperature (ranging from a\nfew to several degrees above), bountiful sunshine (though\nincreasing clouds by mid next week) and dry weather (cumulative\nprobabilities of measurable rainfall remain at/below 10% through\nnext Thursday morning).\n\nMore forecast variations arrive late next week as models show\nlarger uncertainty in ridge placement plus trough movement with\nincreasing chances of a rain-producing system Halloween night. \nBut 24-hour probabilities generally never exceed 50% during this\ntimeframe, suggesting rain likely confined to one period \n(rather than multiple rounds) with models uncertain which of \nThursday/Friday/Saturday sees the best chance.",
